[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317207181","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118923#issuecomment-4317207181","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118923","id":4317207181,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAVNajQ","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T00:28:37Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T00:28:37Z","body":"> The gizmo (and runtime debug collision visualization) for `WorldBoundaryShape3D` shows the inverted `d` value. That is, what's actually happening under the hood is that as `d` increases, the plane is pushed along the _negative_ of the normal. This is the correct and intended behaviour.\n\nThis is not correct. As explained in the Plane docs `d` refers to the `ax + by + cz = d` plane equation. What you're saying would be true for the `ax + by + cz + d = 0` plane equation (they differ by the sign of `d`).\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6d6e822c689acb54bf86e19cc2bbbe3fa567b123/doc/classes/Plane.xml#L154-L157\n\nFor confirmation:\n```gdscript\nvar normal := Vector3.UP\nvar d := 5.0\nprint(Plane(normal, d).intersects_ray(Vector3.ZERO, normal)) # (0.0, 5.0, 0.0)\nprint(Plane(normal, d).intersects_ray(Vector3.ZERO, -normal)) # null\n```\n\nSo the gizmo / debug shape are correct, they match the `plane` set.\nThe bug seems to be Jolt physics misinterpreting the `d` value, for `physics/3d/physics_engine` editor setting set to `GodotPhysics3D` there's no discrepancy between the gizmo/behavior (tested in v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6] and v4.7.beta1.official [1c8cc9e7e]).\n\ncc @mihe","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317207181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317231886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118923#issuecomment-4317231886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118923","id":4317231886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAVO7Dg","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T00:36:46Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T00:36:46Z","body":"> This is not correct. As explained in the Plane docs `d` refers to the `ax + by + cz = d` plane equation. What you're saying would be true for the `ax + by + cz + d = 0` plane equation (they differ by the sign of `d`).\n\nDang, my bad, I assumed `Plane` used `ax + by + cz + d = 0`, since that is what I'm used to from elsewhere. This does seem like an inconsistent treatment of the `d` value between the different physics implementations then. I will update the description to reflect this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317231886/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319509192","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118923#issuecomment-4319509192","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118923","id":4319509192,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAXZ6yA","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}",